{"skill":{"slug":"news-summary","displayName":"News Summary"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1767689990078,"changelog":"- Added detailed documentation of news sources and RSS feed usage, with example `curl` commands for BBC, Reuters, NPR, and Al Jazeera.\n- Clarified workflows for fetching, parsing, and summarizing news headlines, both as text and as short audio using OpenAI TTS.\n- Included example output format for news summaries, grouped by topic.\n- Outlined best practices: concise coverage (5–8 stories), balanced perspectives, and citation guidance.\n- No functional changes to skill logic—documentation only.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2091,"sha256":"1b4c45b56f5675670df484445f9b021b05ba1b2e688c202ac962f22c9812f23b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2084,"sha256":"e678541f886bf934763bcf68f53faa3ce962f080daa5e6f1f7f4077795034735","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015023338,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c66653c903d3b361bb52d5ff71f8102aa1a401292475dd112fabf21beb6a877c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c66653c903d3b361bb52d5ff71f8102aa1a401292475dd112fabf21beb6a877c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: news-summary\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It fetches news from legitimate RSS feeds (BBC, Reuters, NPR, Al Jazeera) using `curl` and processes the content with standard Unix tools (`grep`, `sed`, `head`). It also uses the `$OPENAI_API_KEY` to interact with the OpenAI TTS API for voice summaries, which is a legitimate use case for the skill's stated purpose. There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts in SKILL.md.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159649619},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":18,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789015023338},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This news-summary skill is coherent and purpose-aligned, with minor privacy and temporary-file cautions for optional voice summaries.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network calls to public RSS feeds and the OpenAI TTS API are proportionate for news and voice-summary features, but voice mode transmits generated summary text to a third-party API.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a single non-executable Markdown skill file with no install scripts, packaged code, dependency installation, or tool replacement behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The activation wording is somewhat broad, but the examples and workflow stay within news and current-events requests rather than unrelated agent behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"There is no persistence, privilege escalation, background worker, or credential harvesting; the only local write described is the optional voice output at a fixed /tmp/news.mp3 path.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill only describes fetching public RSS feeds, summarizing news, and optionally creating an audio summary, which matches its stated news-briefing purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Installers should treat this as a public-news helper. Use the voice-summary option only when sending the summary text to OpenAI TTS is acceptable, and consider changing the fixed /tmp/news.mp3 example to a unique private temporary file before operational use.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad trigger language is real but still news-oriented, so it is a routing caution rather than evidence of hidden or purpose-mismatched behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending the generated news summary to OpenAI TTS is consistent with the disclosed voice-summary feature, but users should avoid including private or sensitive text in voice summaries.\n[T09] expected: Creating an audio file is expected for voice output, though using a predictable shared temporary path can cause collisions or local exposure in multi-user environments.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015023338}}}}}